Sources written for this project, not carried by any v10 tape.

    nafsmnt.c   mounts a netfs share.  v10 removed gmount -- slot 49 of its
                system call table reads `nosys / was gmount' -- and fmount
                takes an open file descriptor, so the connection is named by
                the fd.  nafsmnt does what mount(8) cannot: tcp_sock(), then
                tcp_connect(), then fmount(1, fd, mount, dev).  fstab(5) has
                five fields and none of them holds a host or a port, so this
                cannot be reached through /etc/mount -a.

./patch stages it into /v10/usr/src/cmd; the mkfile builds it into /etc,
which is where /etc/rc calls it from.
